# NestJS + GraphQL — Palos de Leños

## Estructura de módulo

Cada feature sigue esta estructura:

```
apps/api/src/
└── <feature>/
    ├── <feature>.module.ts
    ├── resolver/
    │   └── <feature>.resolver.ts        # ObjectTypes, InputTypes y Resolver co-localizados
    ├── service/
    │   └── <feature>.service.ts         # lógica de negocio, orquesta el repository
    ├── repository/
    │   └── <feature>.repository.ts      # acceso directo a PrismaService
    └── interfaces/
        └── <feature>.interfaces.ts      # tipos TypeScript, no GraphQL
```

## Tenant ID

El `tenantId` se extrae del header `x-tenant-id`, **no** de un JWT claim. Usar el helper compartido o un método privado en el resolver:

```typescript
// Opción 1 — helper compartido (preferida)
import { getTenantIdFromContext, type GqlRequestContext } from '../../common/graphql/tenant-from-context';

@Query(() => [RecipeType])
recipes(@Context() context: GqlRequestContext): Promise<Recipe[]> {
  return this.recipeService.findAll(getTenantIdFromContext(context));
}

// Opción 2 — método privado en el resolver
private getTenantId(context: { req?: { headers?: Record<string, unknown> } }): string {
  const tenantId = context.req?.headers?.['x-tenant-id'];
  if (typeof tenantId !== 'string' || !tenantId.trim()) {
    throw new Error('x-tenant-id header is required');
  }
  return tenantId.trim();
}
```

## Autenticación

El proyecto tiene **dos sistemas de auth independientes**:

| Sistema | Para | Guard |
|---|---|---|
| JWT email auth | Global users (backoffice) | `GqlJwtAuthGuard`, `@CurrentUser()` |
| PIN/cédula auth | MES operational users | `MesAuthGuard` o validación en service |

- Rutas públicas: decorar con `@Public()`.
- Rutas JWT: usar `@UseGuards(GqlJwtAuthGuard)` + `@CurrentUser()`.
- Mayoría de resolvers de negocio usan solo `x-tenant-id` header sin JWT guard.

## Resolvers

### Patrón estándar

- ObjectTypes, InputTypes y el Resolver pueden ir co-localizados en el mismo archivo resolver.
- El resolver NO contiene lógica de negocio — delega al service.
- Queries y Mutations separados con comentarios.
- Subscriptions vía `graphql-subscriptions` PubSub para realtime.

```typescript
@ObjectType('WorkStation')
export class WorkStationType {
  @Field(() => ID) id!: string;
  @Field() tenantId!: string;
  @Field() name!: string;
  @Field() code!: string;
  @Field(() => String, { nullable: true }) location?: string;
  @Field() isActive!: boolean;
  @Field() createdAt!: Date;
}

@InputType('CreateWorkStationInput')
export class CreateWorkStationInputDto {
  @Field()
  @IsString()
  @IsNotEmpty()
  name!: string;

  @Field()
  @IsString()
  @IsNotEmpty()
  code!: string;

  @Field(() => String, { nullable: true })
  @IsString()
  @IsOptional()
  location?: string;
}

@Resolver(() => WorkStationType)
export class WorkStationResolver {
  constructor(
    private readonly workStationService: WorkStationService,
    @Inject(PUB_SUB) private readonly pubSub: PubSub,
  ) {}

  // ─── Queries ───────────────────────────────────────────
  @Query(() => [WorkStationType])
  workStations(
    @Context() context: GqlRequestContext,
    @Args('limit', { type: () => Int, nullable: true }) limit?: number,
    @Args('offset', { type: () => Int, nullable: true }) offset?: number,
  ) {
    return this.workStationService.findAll(getTenantIdFromContext(context), { limit, offset });
  }

  @Query(() => WorkStationType, { nullable: true })
  async workStation(
    @Context() context: GqlRequestContext,
    @Args('id', { type: () => ID }) id: string,
  ) {
    try {
      return await this.workStationService.findById(id, getTenantIdFromContext(context));
    } catch {
      return null;
    }
  }

  // ─── Mutations ─────────────────────────────────────────
  @Mutation(() => WorkStationType)
  async createWorkStation(
    @Context() context: GqlRequestContext,
    @Args('input') input: CreateWorkStationInputDto,
  ) {
    const result = await this.workStationService.create(getTenantIdFromContext(context), input);
    await this.pubSub.publish('workStationCreated', { workStationCreated: result });
    return result;
  }

  // ─── Subscriptions ─────────────────────────────────────
  @Subscription(() => WorkStationType)
  workStationCreated(): AsyncIterator<unknown> {
    return this.pubSub.asyncIterator('workStationCreated');
  }
}
```

### ObjectTypes

- Tipado 1:1 con el modelo Prisma.
- Campos sensibles (`passwordHash`, `pinHash`, `cedulaHash`, `refreshToken`): **no exponer** — omitir del ObjectType.
- Usar `@Field(() => Type, { nullable: true })` para campos opcionales.
- Campos `Decimal` de Prisma → `@Field(() => Float)` en GraphQL.

```typescript
@ObjectType('Supplier')
export class SupplierType {
  @Field(() => ID) id!: string;
  @Field() tenantId!: string;
  @Field() razonSocial!: string;
  @Field() nit!: string;
  @Field(() => String, { nullable: true }) dv?: string;
  @Field() isActive!: boolean;
  @Field() createdAt!: Date;
  @Field() updatedAt!: Date;
  // passwordHash, etc. — NUNCA exponer
}
```

## Services

- Inyectar el **Repository** del módulo, no `PrismaService` directamente.
- Manejar errores con excepciones tipadas de NestJS (`NotFoundException`, `ConflictException`, `ForbiddenException`).
- Validar inputs con Zod o `class-validator` según el patrón del módulo.

```typescript
@Injectable()
export class WorkStationService {
  constructor(private readonly workStationRepository: WorkStationRepository) {}

  async findAll(tenantId: string, opts: { limit?: number; offset?: number } = {}) {
    return this.workStationRepository.findAll(tenantId, opts);
  }

  async findById(id: string, tenantId: string) {
    const station = await this.workStationRepository.findById(id, tenantId);
    if (!station) throw new NotFoundException(`WorkStation "${id}" not found`);
    return station;
  }

  async create(tenantId: string, data: unknown) {
    const validated = validate(CreateWorkStationSchema, data);
    return this.workStationRepository.create(tenantId, validated);
  }

  async deactivate(id: string, tenantId: string) {
    await this.findById(id, tenantId);
    return this.workStationRepository.softDelete(id);
  }
}
```

## Repositories

- Repositorio = capa de acceso a datos. Inyecta `PrismaService`.
- Toda query lleva `tenantId` como primer parámetro en modelos multi-tenant.
- Usar `Prisma.ModelWhereInput` para tipado fuerte en filtros.
- Soft delete via `isActive: false` — nunca `prisma.model.delete()`.

```typescript
@Injectable()
export class WorkStationRepository {
  constructor(private readonly prisma: PrismaService) {}

  async findAll(tenantId: string, opts: { limit?: number; offset?: number }) {
    const take = Math.min(Math.max(1, opts.limit ?? DEFAULT_PAGE_SIZE), MAX_PAGE_SIZE);
    const skip = Math.max(0, opts.offset ?? 0);

    return this.prisma.workStation.findMany({
      where: { tenantId, isActive: true },
      take,
      skip,
      orderBy: { name: 'asc' },
    });
  }

  async findById(id: string, tenantId: string) {
    return this.prisma.workStation.findFirst({ where: { id, tenantId } });
  }

  async findByCode(tenantId: string, code: string) {
    return this.prisma.workStation.findUnique({
      where: { tenantId_code: { tenantId, code } },
    });
  }

  async create(tenantId: string, data: CreateWorkStationInput) {
    return this.prisma.workStation.create({ data: { ...data, tenantId } });
  }

  async softDelete(id: string) {
    return this.prisma.workStation.update({ where: { id }, data: { isActive: false } });
  }
}
```

## InputTypes y validación

- Usar `@InputType()` para mutations.
- Validar con `class-validator`. Campos opcionales con `@IsOptional()` explícito.
- Para paginación: `limit` y `offset` (patrón del proyecto, no cursor-based).

```typescript
@InputType('WorkStationFilter')
export class WorkStationFilterDto {
  @Field(() => Int, { nullable: true })
  @IsOptional()
  @IsInt()
  @Min(1)
  @Max(100)
  limit?: number;

  @Field(() => Int, { nullable: true })
  @IsOptional()
  @IsInt()
  @Min(0)
  offset?: number;

  @Field(() => Boolean, { nullable: true })
  @IsOptional()
  @IsBoolean()
  isActive?: boolean;
}
```

## Módulos

- Registrar Repository y Service en `providers`, exportar Service si otros módulos lo necesitan.
- `PUB_SUB` inyectado desde `PubSubModule`.
- `forwardRef()` solo cuando hay dependencia circular real.

```typescript
@Module({
  providers: [WorkStationRepository, WorkStationService, WorkStationResolver],
  exports: [WorkStationService],
})
export class WorkStationModule {}
```

## Anti-patrones prohibidos

- ❌ Lógica de negocio en resolvers — delegar al service
- ❌ PrismaService inyectado en services — usar el repository del módulo
- ❌ `any` en TypeScript — tipos explícitos o `unknown`
- ❌ Queries sin `tenantId` en modelos multi-tenant
- ❌ Exponer `passwordHash`, `pinHash`, `cedulaHash`, `refreshToken` en ObjectTypes
- ❌ `try/catch` silenciosos sin loggear el error
- ❌ `Float` en schema para campos monetarios o de cantidad — usar `Decimal` en Prisma, `Float` solo en el ObjectType de GraphQL
